{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865824-didnt-knew-where-to-post-this-any-chances-for-hol-to-be-re-edited","id":865824,"title":"Didnt knew where to post this: Any chances for HoL to be re edited?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-14T23:50:14-07:00","id":865824,"title":"Didnt knew where to post this: Any chances for HoL to be re edited?","content":"i been collecting the old WW material and i seen a game being mentioned under Black Dog, a game Called Human ocupied Landfield. i have no idea whats about but im curious about it (and why does it deserves to be a Black Dog propierty)<br /> Any chances to have a kickstarter for this one or a re edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T00:18:26-07:00","id":865833,"title":"","content":"HoL was only published by White Wolf under the Black Dog label - they did not own or create it. The rights belong to another company now, or are back with the creators.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T07:42:59-07:00","id":865941,"title":"","content":"<i><b>H\u014dL</b></i> is one of the most insane RPG's I've ever seen. And I've seen a lot. It's a sci-fi gonzo setting in the manner of Warhammer 40 000, Traveller and Fading Suns. It's just that the people writing it were suffering from cartoon levels of ADHD and the idea that every point of the game should be played for comedy.<br /> <br /> So you end up with a RPG in which...<ul><li>there are no Character creation rules (they come in the supplement <i><b>Butt</b></i>ery <i><b>H\u014dL</b></i>esomeness, with more tables then you could possibly imagine, and with worse results then Traveller <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - they were most likely never meant to be used in any way but provoking utter stomach curling laughter),</li> <li>The sample characters are a psychotic potato that wants vengeance for the systematic genocide of his kind, a brain in a jar swissknife, the silver surfer if he replaced the angst with all american suburbian mentality, Elvis (of course the Aliens took him), a insane over the top power armored pope that puts fear into the hearts of men... and young boys...</li> <li>Where clowns and mimes may be the deadliest men and women in the universe... or are they?</li> <li>where all the skills are painfully obvious like <i>&quot;Make Sharp Things Go Through Soft Things That Scream and Bleed&quot;, &quot;Sounding More Important Than God Allmighty&quot; </i>or maybe<i> &quot;Turn Radios into Howitzers&quot;, </i></li> <li>where the writers literally go on a batshit ramble on things utterly unrelated to anything else or start rolling their text into whirls, onto margins or all around everything... and there is that whole part of ButtHoll where they literally go and create a small LARP set for rules for playing pimps and crackaddicts and how their life looks</li> <li>this book is probably pure agony to reprint because it's not gonna go through OCR very well... most of it is handwritten in bizzare handdrawn fonts with very little rhyme or reason, and art and text blend utter abandon</li> <li>A money system based on a ripening mushroom that gains value the longer you hold on it... just be careful because after a while IT WILL EAT YOU AND THE WHOLE PLANET YOU ARE ON, WITH THEIR GIANT GNASHING TEETH!</li> <li>An insanely complex celestial imperial bureaucracy gets a ton of pages only to be completley ignored because the core precept of the game is that you are essentially dropped on the single worst hellhole you can ever imagine</li> <li>Religion is franchished more then fast food, and it has actually merged in many cases</li> <li>You actually arm yourself with bizzare weapons like the Grenade of Monkeys, Chainsaw YoYos and such brilliant weapons of mass destruction (and distraction) like Kitty Kitty Bang Bang (yes, it's a kitten, yes it's strapped with more explosives then it weighs, yes it goes bang) or maybe The Can of Mace, which literally sprays out Maces.</li> </ul><br /> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/7iB8w\" target=\"_blank\">... it's... special. Here's a couple of pages I've tossed online before, I can put some more up when I have the books at hand...</a><br /> <br /> The only reason it's Black Dog is because you really don't want it to get into the hands of anyone who might take it even remotely seriously, as it's probably one of the most insane RPG's written for sane people. For reference, this is the kidn of characters we have had made from this mayhem:<ul><li>a man who wanted to unleash his inner woman - so he cut off half his body and replaced it with a female cyborg prosthesis</li> <li>a naked hobo who walked around with a coat made of hundreds of different radios all tuned to different stations</li> <li>an Iguana that was convinced it was actually human, and always discussed the philosophical hardships of how much being a human sucked</li> <li>a Psionic whale in a giant fishtank</li> <li>a space pirate who ran the local McDonalds variant which served overipe cash on a kebab</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 04-15-2016, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T23:02:24-07:00","id":866270,"title":"","content":"I used to own both books and I kick myself every time I think about it and I wish I had never sold it! It would probably never get played but it was hysterical just to read. I would happily back a Kickstarter for a new version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T08:11:23-07:00","id":868443,"title":"","content":"Can I buy either of these books anywhere